winewayland: tray menus open where the user clicked (layer-shell placement, Plasma's ContextMenu path), and tray polish.

On 180 (patches 123 + 124) a tray menu that is not a Win32 menu, such as Filmora 16's Qt tray menu (Open / Screen
Recorder / Exit) or a program's own popup window, did not open at the icon on Plasma. It went through the dbusmenu
request, which carries no click point, so the program placed it at a stale cursor. As an xdg_toplevel KWin centered it,
listed it in the taskbar, or closed it again at once. Plasma was meanwhile left holding an empty menu that swallowed the
next click. sway and Hyprland tiled such a menu window to fill the screen. On the dbusmenu path every program got its
right click at 0,0. Balloons showed the item id ("wine-<class>-<id>") as the application name. His calls: C178 (menus
at the icon), C179 ("Go for it": non-Win32 menus at the pointer where the compositor allows it, GNOME as it is).

Windows: explorer puts the cursor on the icon before the tray callback, and the program opens its menu at GetCursorPos
(or at the NOTIFYICON_VERSION_4 anchor). A Win32 menu, a Qt QMenu and a program's own popup all land at the click, on
top, with the keyboard, and close on Escape, on a choice, or when a click elsewhere takes the foreground.

What changes:
- window.c / wayland_surface.c: the topmost captionless popups a program shows within 2 s of a tray click explorer
  relayed to it, and further ones while such a menu is open (its submenus), become zwlr_layer_shell_v1 surfaces where
  the compositor offers it (KWin, sway, Hyprland, labwc; not GNOME): overlay layer of their output, anchored top-left at
  the window's own Win32 position, keyboard focus on demand (protocol v4). No exclusive keyboard grab and no surface over
  the rest of the screen, so a hung program cannot hold the desktop; a click elsewhere takes the keyboard focus away and
  the program closes its menu as on Windows. explorer marks the click on the desktop window (process id and time).
- wayland_sni.c, Plasma (XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP contains KDE, layer-shell present): an icon starts with Menu
  "/NO_DBUSMENU", so Plasma calls ContextMenu(x, y) with the click point and the program puts its menu there. explorer
  also tags the icon's window for that click: if the program's TrackPopupMenu offers a Win32 menu, explorer refuses it
  (the menu opens at the click now, as the program's own window) and announces the item again under a new name with the
  dbusmenu, so from the next right click Plasma draws the menu at the icon (124). A program that never shows a Win32 menu
  stays on ContextMenu: no empty Plasma menu, nothing to swallow the next click. Other trays (GNOME's extension, XFCE,
  waybar) only offer the dbusmenu: unchanged.
- The dbusmenu path relays the right click at the last point any tray gave for that icon (else for any icon), with the
  cursor there, instead of 0,0.
- A balloon's application name is the first line of the icon's tip (tray programs put their name there), else the id.

Not covered:
- XFCE and waybar (libdbusmenu-gtk) still draw the first menu of an icon in a popup sized for 124's one-item
  placeholder (a scroll arrow); from the second open the full menu. The host sizes its popup from the layout it holds
  before it asks the program, and Windows asks the program only on the click.
- XFCE and waybar send no "closed": after Escape or a click elsewhere the program stays in TrackPopupMenu (pumping its
  messages) until the next right click. There is no signal to end it on; not changed.
- GNOME: no layer-shell, so a non-Win32 tray menu is placed by mutter as before. GNOME and XFCE give no click point, so
  without a prior Activate/ContextMenu the program still gets 0,0 on the dbusmenu path.
- Plasma, the first right click of a program that uses Win32 menus: its menu opens at the click in the Neutron Win32
  style, not Plasma's; the re-announcement can move the icon within the tray once.
- sway and Hyprland not run with this patch (their tiling of the menu window is INFERRED gone: layer surfaces are not
  tiled). The balloon name is not the exe's version-info name.

Lab, 180 + this (lab 11.10-180t), nested Plasma 6 on a lab desk's own bus (agents/trayv2):
- Filmora 16's Qt tray menu: at the icon on the first right click of a fresh launch 2/2 (and on reopen 3/3); Escape
  closes 2/2, a click elsewhere 1/1, "Open Wondershare Filmora" 1/1; the next right click always opened (no swallowed
  click). NEUTRON_TRAY_POPUP_LAYER=0, same build: no menu at all, as on 180 (1/1).
- traytest, its own popup window: at the click 3/3, Escape / elsewhere / "Custom B" 1/1 each, never a dbusmenu.
- traytest, Win32 menu: first right click at the click 2/2, Escape 0 2/2; item announced again with the dbusmenu 2/2;
  the second right click Plasma's own menu at the icon 2/2, "Second" returned 2; the program got the click point
  (3318,2105 device) on the dbusmenu path. NEUTRON_TRAY_POPUP_LAYER=0: Plasma's menu from the first click, 0,0 (180).
- Podman desktops (agents/desktops): GNOME 51 + AppIndicator: menu at the icon on the first open, "Second" 2, Escape 0
  (as 180); XFCE (labwc + xfce4-panel): first open the placeholder-sized popup, second open the full menu (as 180).

Kill switch NEUTRON_TRAY_POPUP_LAYER=0 (layer placement and the Plasma ContextMenu path); 123/124's are unchanged.

